# Dependencies
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# Build artifacts
dist/
target/
# A second cargo target tree (`src-tauri/target-verify2/`, 1.3 GB of the same build output) is what an
# out-of-line CARGO_TARGET_DIR leaves behind when a verification build must not clobber the tree the
# application runs from. It is build output like `target/`, so the whole family is ignored rather than
# one spelling; check:size and check:links walk untracked-but-not-ignored files and would otherwise
# measure generated bindgen output.
src-tauri/target-*/
*.tsbuildinfo
src-tauri/binaries/
# SDK host:编译输入树（junction/还原产物）与 standalone 产物都是构建中间物
host/.build/
host/dist/
# host 的开发期数据根与验证产物（原始日志/快照/体积与 sha256）同样不入库
host/.dev-data/
host/evidence/

# Environment and local files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.local

# IDE and OS files
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.log
coverage/

# Verification scaffolds: measurement harnesses, their raw output and pane prompts.
# These are development-time artifacts, never part of the product; see rules.md §11.
# Keep them out of the repository entirely (delete them, or leave them untracked here).
# The patterns cover files as well as directories, and the dot-prefixed spellings too: a
# screenshot written beside them (`probe-app.png`, `.probe-app.png`) is the same kind of
# artifact as one written inside them, and the earlier `probe-*/` form ignored only the
# directory case.
probe-*
.probe-*
perf-*
.perf-*
.tmp-*
# A tool that joined a path without its separator (`C:\project\omp-desktop.tmp-a.png` arrived as
# `projectomp-desktop.tmp-a.png` beside the project root) leaves a screenshot named `*.tmp-*`.
# 7a7444b committed one; this is the same measurement artifact under a different spelling.
*.tmp-*
/%TEMP%clippy-after.txt
/buildtests.out
/test.out

# `notes/` is local-only: decision records stay on the machine that wrote them and never enter the
# repository. An ignore rule cannot untrack what git already carries, so this takes effect only
# once the directory is out of the index (`git rm -r --cached notes`); while a note is still
# tracked, a pathspec under the ignored directory is refused and a changed note cannot be staged
# (2026-10-31). `check:note-format` skips the directory when it is absent, so a clone without it
# still passes.
notes/

# Windows paths that a shell escaped into a *directory name*.
# A command run with `C:\Users\…\AppData\Local\Volta` as its cwd had `:` and `\` remapped to the
# private-use characters U+F03A / U+F05C, so Windows accepted the whole path as one directory and a
# tool (Volta) wrote its cache into it. It landed inside `src/` once (committed by 264cb74) and is
# never product content. The pattern spells the remapped separators as `*` rather than `?`: git
# matches `?` per byte, and each of those two characters is three bytes of UTF-8, so a `?`-per-
# character pattern never matches. Nothing else in the tree carries this sequence of segments.
C*Users*Administrator*AppData*Local*Volta/
